> It shouldn't be _too_ difficult to write a savelog file, prefereable in the
> same structure as the logfile, each time a player saves. 

It would have to be more often than that; with a high-speed connection it is 
possible to never save.  Heck, even my dialup connection (in a house with 
terrible phone lines) can stay online several days, depending on luck.

What I think you'd need to do is write a small information file every time 
the player saves or changes dungeon level.  When he dies or ascends the file 
would be deleted.  It should include:

- race, class, sex
- character level and max hitpoints
- current and max dungeon level reached
- turns used
- current conducts
- the score 
- Flag A: set if the player has reached the Castle or Valley
- Flag B: set if he has performed the Invocation

And the master server would collect the information files, and they would 
appear on each player's information page along with his completed games. 

Games with Flag A set would be considered potential ascensions, and appear on 
the trophy page, but in red text.  Games with Flag B set would also have a 
small icon indicating that the player is (probably) close to ascension.


